IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eca-nouns`
IMPORT `eca-schedules`
IMPORT `eca-part1-preliminary`

-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: PART 2, MEDIATION OF EMPLOYMENT DISPUTES (ss 3 to 7).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.  Target compiler: main (build 109).
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is a yes the Act gives; JUST FALSE is a no the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- Amounts and periods the Act leaves to regulations, orders or Rules of Court are MAYBE inputs: NOTHING when not given.
-- A period "N months after" a date is counted with `add months` (daydate), which clamps to the last day of a shorter month (fork F6 in NOTES.md).
-- s 3(6) and (7) and s 4(6) are regulation-making and order-making powers (machinery, inert, reason 2): the Act's own periods (6 months, one year) are used as printed, and an order under s 3(7) would change the answers.

§ `Part 2 -- Mediation of employment disputes`

§§ `s 3 -- the mediation request`

-- s 3(8): this section does not apply to a claim if a tripartite mediation has been conducted.
-- src:501 | (8) This section does not apply to a claim if a tripartite mediation
-- src:502 | has been conducted in an endeavour to reach a settlement in respect of
-- src:503 | the specified employment disputes to which the claim relates.
@ref s 3(8) (src:501-503)
GIVEN `a tripartite mediation has been conducted in an endeavour to reach a settlement of the specified employment disputes to which the claim relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(8) section 3 does not apply to the claim` MEANS
    IF `a tripartite mediation has been conducted in an endeavour to reach a settlement of the specified employment disputes to which the claim relates`
    -- (the text says it in so many words: "This section does not apply to a claim if a tripartite mediation has been conducted")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a claim if a tripartite mediation has been conducted" (none has been, so section 3 applies; the "if" rule of 2026-10-29)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 3(1): before lodging a claim, the claimant must submit a mediation request listing every specified employment dispute the claim is lodged for.
-- src:326 | 3.—(1) Before a claimant lodges a claim against a respondent, the
-- src:327 | claimant must submit to the Commissioner a mediation request
-- src:328 | relating to every specified employment dispute for which the claim
-- src:329 | will be lodged.
@ref s 3(1) (src:326-329)
GIVEN `the claim will be lodged for a specified employment dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a tripartite mediation has been conducted in an endeavour to reach a settlement of the specified employment disputes to which the claim relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the claimant must submit a mediation request before lodging the claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a claim if a tripartite mediation has been conducted" (s 3(8))
        IF `s 3(8) section 3 does not apply to the claim` `a tripartite mediation has been conducted in an endeavour to reach a settlement of the specified employment disputes to which the claim relates` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the claim will be lodged for a specified employment dispute` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled I(c)]: the duty is to submit a request "relating to every specified employment dispute for which the claim will be lodged"; a claim lodged for none is not spoken to
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 3(1): the mediation request must relate to every specified employment dispute for which the claim will be lodged.
-- src:326 | 3.—(1) Before a claimant lodges a claim against a respondent, the
-- src:327 | claimant must submit to the Commissioner a mediation request
-- src:328 | relating to every specified employment dispute for which the claim
-- src:329 | will be lodged.
@ref s 3(1) (src:326-329)
GIVEN `the number of specified employment disputes for which the claim will be lodged` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those disputes that the mediation request relates to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the mediation request relates to every specified employment dispute for which the claim will be lodged` MEANS
    IF `the number of those disputes that the mediation request relates to` AT LEAST `the number of specified employment disputes for which the claim will be lodged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant must submit to the Commissioner a mediation request relating to every specified employment dispute for which the claim will be lodged" (a dispute is left out)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 3(1) with s 3(2), as a regulative rule: the claimant MUST submit the mediation request, within the number of days that s 3(2) allows from the date its time limit counts from.
-- The Act states no sanction for lateness in this rule: BREACH below only marks that the time passed without the act (consequences are in s 3(4)(a) and s 12(5)).
-- src:326 | 3.—(1) Before a claimant lodges a claim against a respondent, the
-- src:327 | claimant must submit to the Commissioner a mediation request
-- src:328 | relating to every specified employment dispute for which the claim
-- src:329 | will be lodged.
-- src:331 | (2) The mediation request must be submitted to the Commissioner
-- src:332 | in the prescribed manner by the following time:
@ref s 3(1) and (2) (src:326-332)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed by section 3(2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 3(1) and (2) the claimant's duty to submit a mediation request` MEANS
    PARTY Claimant
    MUST `submit a mediation request`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed by section 3(2)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Claimant BECAUSE "the mediation request was not submitted to the Commissioner by the time section 3(2) gives"

§§ `s 3(2) -- the time limit for the request`

-- s 3(2)(a): salary recovery under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968: within the period in section 65(2A) of that Act or, if extended under section 65(2B), the extended period.  That Act is not among the sources, so the last day of that (possibly extended) period is an input.
-- src:334 | (a) for any specified employment dispute concerning the
-- src:335 | recovery, under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968, of
-- src:336 | salary — within the period mentioned in section 65(2A) of
-- src:337 | that Act or, if that period is extended under section 65(2B)
-- src:338 | of that Act, within the extended period;
@ref s 3(2)(a) (src:334-338)
GIVEN `the last day of the period in section 65(2A) of the Employment Act 1968, as extended under section 65(2B)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 3(2)(a) the last day for a request about recovering salary under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the period in section 65(2A) of the Employment Act 1968, as extended under section 65(2B)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period is "mentioned in section 65(2A) of that Act", which is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST day THEN JUST day

-- s 3(2)(b): re-employment dispute described in section 8A(3) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993: not later than 6 months after the last day of employment.
-- src:340 | (b) for any re‑employment dispute described in section 8A(3)
-- src:341 | of the Retirement and Re‑employment Act 1993 — not
-- src:342 | later than 6 months after the last day of employment of the
-- src:343 | employee;
@ref s 3(2)(b) (src:340-343)
GIVEN `the last day of employment of the employee` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 3(2)(b) the last day for a request about a re-employment dispute described in section 8A(3) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of employment of the employee`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph counts from the last day of employment and none was given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`add months` day 6)

-- s 3(2)(c): re-employment dispute under section 8B(7): within the time determined under section 8B(8) of that Act.
-- src:345 | (c) for any re‑employment dispute under section 8B(7) of the
-- src:346 | Retirement and Re‑employment Act 1993 — within the
-- src:347 | time determined under section 8B(8) of that Act;
@ref s 3(2)(c) (src:345-347)
GIVEN `the last day of the time determined under section 8B(8) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 3(2)(c) the last day for a request about a re-employment dispute under section 8B(7) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the time determined under section 8B(8) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the time is "determined under section 8B(8) of that Act", which is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST day THEN JUST day

-- s 3(2)(d): wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of the Employment Act 1968: not later than one month after the date of the dismissal.
-- src:349 | (d) for any wrongful dismissal dispute in relation to which an
-- src:350 | employee may lodge a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of
-- src:355 | the Employment Act 1968 — not later than one month
-- src:356 | after the date of the dismissal of the employee;
@ref s 3(2)(d) (src:349-356)
GIVEN `the date of the dismissal of the employee` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 3(2)(d) the last day for a request about a wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of the Employment Act 1968` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date of the dismissal of the employee`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph counts from the date of the dismissal and none was given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`add months` day 1)

-- s 3(2)(e): wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968: within 2 months after the date of the employee's confinement.
-- src:358 | (e) for any wrongful dismissal dispute in relation to which a
-- src:359 | female employee may lodge a claim mentioned in
-- src:360 | section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968 — within
-- src:361 | 2 months after the date of the employee’s confinement;
@ref s 3(2)(e) (src:358-361)
GIVEN `the date of the employee's confinement` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 3(2)(e) the last day for a request about a wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date of the employee's confinement`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph counts from the date of confinement and none was given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`add months` day 2)

-- s 3(2)(f): any other specified employment dispute, where an employment relationship has ended: not later than 6 months after the last day of employment.
-- src:363 | (f) for any specified employment dispute (not being a dispute
-- src:364 | mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)) where an
-- src:365 | employment relationship has ended (whether due to the
-- src:366 | retirement of the employee, or the expiry or termination of
-- src:367 | the contract of service, or otherwise) — not later than
-- src:368 | 6 months after the last day of employment of the employee;
@ref s 3(2)(f) (src:363-368)
GIVEN `the last day of employment of the employee` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 3(2)(f) the last day for a request about another specified employment dispute after the employment relationship has ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of employment of the employee`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph counts from the last day of employment and none was given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`add months` day 6)

-- s 3(2)(g): any other specified employment dispute: not later than one year after the date on which the material facts giving rise to the earliest specified employment dispute listed in the request occurred.
-- src:370 | (g) for any other specified employment dispute — not later
-- src:371 | than one year after the date on which the material facts
-- src:372 | giving rise to the earliest specified employment dispute
-- src:373 | listed in the mediation request occurred.
@ref s 3(2)(g) (src:370-373)
GIVEN `the date on which the material facts giving rise to the earliest specified employment dispute listed in the mediation request occurred` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 3(2)(g) the last day for a request about any other specified employment dispute` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the material facts giving rise to the earliest specified employment dispute listed in the mediation request occurred`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph counts from the date the material facts occurred and none was given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`add years` day 1)

-- s 3(2): the paragraph that applies.  Paragraphs (a) to (e) name the kind of dispute; (f) and (g) are the rest, split by whether the employment relationship has ended ("not being a dispute mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)").
-- src:331 | (2) The mediation request must be submitted to the Commissioner
-- src:332 | in the prescribed manner by the following time:
-- src:334 | (a) for any specified employment dispute concerning the
-- src:335 | recovery, under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968, of
-- src:336 | salary — within the period mentioned in section 65(2A) of
-- src:337 | that Act or, if that period is extended under section 65(2B)
-- src:338 | of that Act, within the extended period;
-- src:340 | (b) for any re‑employment dispute described in section 8A(3)
-- src:341 | of the Retirement and Re‑employment Act 1993 — not
-- src:342 | later than 6 months after the last day of employment of the
-- src:343 | employee;
-- src:345 | (c) for any re‑employment dispute under section 8B(7) of the
-- src:346 | Retirement and Re‑employment Act 1993 — within the
-- src:347 | time determined under section 8B(8) of that Act;
-- src:349 | (d) for any wrongful dismissal dispute in relation to which an
-- src:350 | employee may lodge a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of
-- src:355 | the Employment Act 1968 — not later than one month
-- src:356 | after the date of the dismissal of the employee;
-- src:358 | (e) for any wrongful dismissal dispute in relation to which a
-- src:359 | female employee may lodge a claim mentioned in
-- src:360 | section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968 — within
-- src:361 | 2 months after the date of the employee’s confinement;
-- src:363 | (f) for any specified employment dispute (not being a dispute
-- src:364 | mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)) where an
-- src:365 | employment relationship has ended (whether due to the
-- src:366 | retirement of the employee, or the expiry or termination of
-- src:367 | the contract of service, or otherwise) — not later than
-- src:368 | 6 months after the last day of employment of the employee;
-- src:370 | (g) for any other specified employment dispute — not later
-- src:371 | than one year after the date on which the material facts
-- src:372 | giving rise to the earliest specified employment dispute
-- src:373 | listed in the mediation request occurred.
@ref s 3(2) (src:331-373)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the mediation request time limit`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 3(2) the last day by which the mediation request must be submitted` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's kind
    WHEN `Recovery of salary under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968` THEN
        `s 3(2)(a) the last day for a request about recovering salary under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968` (facts's `the last day of the period in section 65(2A) of the Employment Act 1968, as extended under section 65(2B)`)
    WHEN `Re-employment dispute described in section 8A(3) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` THEN
        `s 3(2)(b) the last day for a request about a re-employment dispute described in section 8A(3) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` (facts's `the last day of employment of the employee`)
    WHEN `Re-employment dispute under section 8B(7) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` THEN
        `s 3(2)(c) the last day for a request about a re-employment dispute under section 8B(7) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` (facts's `the last day of the time determined under section 8B(8) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`)
    WHEN `Wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of the Employment Act 1968` THEN
        `s 3(2)(d) the last day for a request about a wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of the Employment Act 1968` (facts's `the date of the dismissal of the employee`)
    WHEN `Wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968` THEN
        `s 3(2)(e) the last day for a request about a wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968` (facts's `the date of the employee's confinement`)
    WHEN `Another specified employment dispute` THEN
        IF facts's `the employment relationship has ended`
        THEN `s 3(2)(f) the last day for a request about another specified employment dispute after the employment relationship has ended` (facts's `the last day of employment of the employee`)
        ELSE `s 3(2)(g) the last day for a request about any other specified employment dispute` (facts's `the date on which the material facts giving rise to the earliest specified employment dispute listed in the mediation request occurred`)

-- s 3(2): "must be submitted ... by the following time".  A request submitted after the last day does not meet the requirement.
-- src:331 | (2) The mediation request must be submitted to the Commissioner
-- src:332 | in the prescribed manner by the following time:
@ref s 3(2) (src:331-332)
GIVEN `the last day by which the mediation request must be submitted` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the mediation request is submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) the mediation request is submitted by the time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day by which the mediation request must be submitted`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the last day could not be worked out from the facts given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST day THEN
        IF `the date the mediation request is submitted` AT MOST day
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The mediation request must be submitted to the Commissioner in the prescribed manner by the following time"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 3(3) -- what the request must and must not list, and the fee`

-- s 3(3)(a): the request must list every specified employment dispute for which all of (i), (ii) and (iii) are satisfied when it is submitted (subject to (b) and (c)).
-- src:377 | (3) The mediation request —
-- src:379 | (a) subject to paragraphs (b) and (c), must list every specified
-- src:380 | employment dispute in relation to which all of the
-- src:381 | following requirements are satisfied at the time the
-- src:382 | mediation request is submitted to the Commissioner:
-- src:384 | (i) if there is a claim for an amount relating to the
-- src:385 | dispute, that claim satisfies the requirements in
-- src:386 | section 12(2), (3) and (4);
-- src:388 | (ii) the material facts giving rise to the dispute occurred
-- src:389 | not earlier than one year before the date on which
-- src:390 | that request is submitted to the Commissioner in
-- src:391 | accordance with subsection (2);
-- src:393 | (iii) the dispute is not listed in an earlier mediation
-- src:394 | request (relating to specified employment disputes
-- src:395 | between the same claimant and the respondent)
-- src:396 | already accepted by the Commissioner and is not
-- src:397 | withdrawn before the date of the first mediation
-- src:402 | session to be conducted pursuant to the earlier
-- src:403 | mediation request;
@ref s 3(3)(a) (src:377-403)
GIVEN `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that claim satisfies the requirements in section 12(2), (3) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the material facts giving rise to the dispute occurred` IS A DATE
      `the date the mediation request is submitted` IS A DATE
      `the dispute is listed in an earlier mediation request between the same claimant and respondent already accepted by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dispute is withdrawn before the date of the first mediation session to be conducted pursuant to the earlier request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3)(a) the mediation request must list the specified employment dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) the material facts giving rise to the dispute occurred not earlier than one year before the date on which that request is submitted" [ruled I(a)] (the facts are more than one year before the request)
        IF `add years` `the date the material facts giving rise to the dispute occurred` 1 LESS THAN `the date the mediation request is submitted` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF     (    (NOT `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute`)
                 OR `that claim satisfies the requirements in section 12(2), (3) and (4)`)
           AND (    (NOT `the dispute is listed in an earlier mediation request between the same claimant and respondent already accepted by the Commissioner`)
                 OR `the dispute is withdrawn before the date of the first mediation session to be conducted pursuant to the earlier request`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: the duty to list is for a dispute "in relation to which all of the following requirements are satisfied"; when (i) or (iii) is not, the text may be read as a scope limit with no "only"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 3(3)(b): the request must not list a dispute if (i) (a) requires an earlier request, submitted by the claimant and accepted by the Commissioner, to list it; and (ii) the requirements prescribed for this sub-paragraph are not satisfied.
-- src:405 | (b) must not list a specified employment dispute if —
-- src:407 | (i) paragraph (a) requires an earlier mediation request
-- src:408 | that was submitted by the claimant and accepted by
-- src:409 | the Commissioner to list the dispute; and
-- src:411 | (ii) the requirements prescribed for this sub‑paragraph
-- src:412 | are not satisfied in relation to the dispute;
@ref s 3(3)(b) (src:405-412)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) requires an earlier mediation request, submitted by the claimant and accepted by the Commissioner, to list the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements prescribed for this sub-paragraph are satisfied in relation to the dispute` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3)(b) the mediation request must not list the specified employment dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not list a specified employment dispute if" (i) and (ii) both hold; (i) does not
        IF (NOT `paragraph (a) requires an earlier mediation request, submitted by the claimant and accepted by the Commissioner, to list the dispute`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the requirements prescribed for this sub-paragraph" are in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `the requirements prescribed for this sub-paragraph are satisfied in relation to the dispute` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        IF `the requirements prescribed for this sub-paragraph are satisfied in relation to the dispute` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not list a specified employment dispute if" (ii) the prescribed requirements are not satisfied; here they are
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 3(3)(c): the request must not list a dispute if there is a claim for an amount relating to it and, under section 16, that claim cannot be lodged by the claimant with a tribunal.
-- src:414 | (c) must not list a specified employment dispute if —
-- src:416 | (i) there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute;
-- src:417 | and
-- src:419 | (ii) under section 16, that claim cannot be lodged by the
-- src:420 | claimant with a tribunal; and
@ref s 3(3)(c) (src:414-420)
GIVEN `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under section 16 that claim cannot be lodged by the claimant with a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3)(c) the mediation request must not list the specified employment dispute` MEANS
    IF `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` AND `under section 16 that claim cannot be lodged by the claimant with a tribunal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not list a specified employment dispute if" there is a claim for an amount and section 16 bars lodging it; at least one of those is not so
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 3(3)(d): the request must be accompanied by the prescribed fee.  The fee is prescribed by regulations (s 3(6)(d)), so it is an input.
-- src:422 | (d) must be accompanied by the prescribed fee for a mediation
-- src:423 | under this Part.
@ref s 3(3)(d) (src:422-423)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee that accompanies the mediation request` IS A NUMBER
      `the fee prescribed for a mediation under this Part` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3)(d) the mediation request is accompanied by the prescribed fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fee prescribed for a mediation under this Part`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the prescribed fee" is set by regulations under section 3(6)(d), which are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fee THEN
        IF `the amount of the fee that accompanies the mediation request` AT LEAST fee
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by the prescribed fee for a mediation under this Part"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 3(4) and (5) -- what the Commissioner may and must do`

-- s 3(4)(a): the Commissioner may refuse to accept the request if (i) it does not comply with (2) and (3), or (ii) the requirement in section 12(7) cannot be satisfied in relation to that claim.
-- src:427 | (4) The Commissioner may —
-- src:429 | (a) refuse to accept a mediation request if —
-- src:431 | (i) that request does not comply with the requirements
-- src:432 | in subsections (2) and (3); or
-- src:434 | (ii) the requirement in section 12(7) cannot be satisfied
-- src:435 | in relation to that claim;
@ref s 3(4)(a) (src:427-435)
GIVEN `the request complies with the requirements in subsections (2) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement in section 12(7) can be satisfied in relation to that claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(4)(a) the Commissioner may refuse to accept the mediation request` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the request complies with the requirements in subsections (2) and (3)`) OR (NOT `the requirement in section 12(7) can be satisfied in relation to that claim`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "refuse to accept a mediation request if" (i) it does not comply, or (ii) section 12(7) cannot be satisfied; neither holds
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 3(4)(b): the Commissioner may waive, remit or refund, wholly or in part, the fee.  The grant has no condition.
-- src:437 | (b) waive, remit or refund, wholly or in part, the fee mentioned
-- src:438 | in subsection (3)(d); and
@ref s 3(4)(b) (src:437-438)
`s 3(4)(b) the Commissioner may waive, remit or refund the fee` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- s 3(4)(c): the Commissioner may pay the whole or a part of the fee to a person prescribed, or in a prescribed class, in lieu of the Consolidated Fund.
-- src:440 | (c) pay the whole or a part of the fee mentioned in
-- src:441 | subsection (3)(d) to a person who is prescribed, or who
-- src:442 | belongs to a class of persons that is prescribed, in lieu of
-- src:443 | the Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 3(4)(c) (src:440-443)
GIVEN `the person is prescribed, or belongs to a class of persons that is prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(4)(c) the Commissioner may pay the whole or a part of the fee to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is prescribed, or belongs to a class of persons that is prescribed`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is "prescribed" is in regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST prescribed THEN
        IF prescribed
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled I(c)]: the grant is "to a person who is prescribed, or who belongs to a class of persons that is prescribed"; the clause names who may be paid and carries no "only"
        ELSE NOTHING

-- s 3(5): upon accepting the request, the Commissioner must, as soon as reasonably practicable, refer every specified employment dispute listed in it for mediation by an approved mediator.
-- src:445 | (5) Upon accepting the mediation request, the Commissioner must,
-- src:446 | as soon as reasonably practicable, refer every specified employment
-- src:447 | dispute listed in that request for mediation by an approved mediator.
