GIVEN `the Commissioner has accepted the mediation request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dispute is listed in the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(5) the Commissioner must refer the specified employment dispute for mediation by an approved mediator` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon accepting the mediation request" [ruled II(c)] (the Commissioner has not accepted it)
        IF (NOT `the Commissioner has accepted the mediation request`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the dispute is listed in the request` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled I(c)]: the duty is to refer "every specified employment dispute listed in" the request; a dispute not listed is not spoken to
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 3(5) as a regulative rule.  The Act gives no time but "as soon as reasonably practicable", so the rule has no WITHIN: the obligation stands until the act is done.
-- src:445 | (5) Upon accepting the mediation request, the Commissioner must,
-- src:446 | as soon as reasonably practicable, refer every specified employment
-- src:447 | dispute listed in that request for mediation by an approved mediator.
@ref s 3(5) (src:445-447)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 3(5) the Commissioner's duty to refer the listed disputes for mediation` MEANS
    PARTY Commissioner
    MUST `refer every listed specified employment dispute for mediation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Commissioner BECAUSE "the listed disputes were not referred for mediation by an approved mediator"

