GIVEN `it is a limited liability partnership as defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(5) the entity is a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `it is a limited liability partnership as defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“body corporate” includes a limited liability partnership"; the text does not say what else is a body corporate
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 5(5): "officer", in relation to a body corporate, means a director, partner, member of the committee of management, chief executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer.
-- src:605 | “officer”, in relation to a body corporate, means a director,
-- src:606 | partner, member of the committee of management, chief
-- src:607 | executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the
-- src:608 | body corporate.
@ref s 5(5) “officer” (src:605-608)
GIVEN position IS A `Position in a body corporate`
      `the position is similar to those listed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `Director` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Member of the committee of management` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Chief executive` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Manager` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Another position` THEN
        IF `the position is similar to those listed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“officer”, in relation to a body corporate, means a director, partner, member of the committee of management, chief executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 5(1) to (4): who may represent a party at a mediation under this Part.  s 5(1) says a party must act in person and cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor or by an agent, except as (2) and (3) provide.
-- (2): a party other than an individual may be represented (a) if the Government, by a public officer; (b) if a body corporate, by an officer or a full-time employee; (c) if a partnership, by a partner or a full-time employee; (d) if an unincorporated association, by a member of the governing body or a full-time employee; (e) by any other individual prescribed by regulations.
-- (3): a party who is an individual may be represented by any other individual prescribed by regulations.
-- src:562 | 5.—(1) Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3), a party to a
-- src:563 | mediation under this Part —
-- src:565 | (a) must act in person;
-- src:567 | (b) cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor; and
-- src:569 | (c) cannot be represented by an agent, whether paid or
-- src:570 | otherwise.
-- src:572 | (2) A party other than an individual may be represented —
-- src:574 | (a) if the party is the Government, by a public officer;
-- src:576 | (b) if the party is a body corporate, by an officer, or a full‑time
-- src:577 | employee, of the body corporate;
-- src:579 | (c) if the party is a partnership, by a partner, or a full‑time
-- src:580 | employee, of the partnership;
-- src:582 | (d) if the party is an unincorporated association, by a member
-- src:583 | of the governing body, or a full‑time employee, of the
-- src:584 | unincorporated association; or
-- src:586 | (e) by any other individual prescribed by regulations made
-- src:587 | under section 34.
-- src:589 | (3) A party who is an individual may be represented by any other
-- src:590 | individual prescribed by regulations made under section 34.
-- src:592 | (4) For the purposes of subsections (2)(e) and (3), the regulations
-- src:593 | made under section 34 may prescribe different individuals for
-- src:594 | different parties and different circumstances.
@ref s 5(1) to (4) (src:562-594)
GIVEN party IS A `Kind of party`
      representative IS A `Kind of representative`
      `the regulations prescribe the representative for the party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) to (3) the party may be represented at the mediation by the representative` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- (2)(a)
        IF party EQUALS `The Government` AND representative EQUALS `A public officer` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (2)(b)
        IF party EQUALS `A body corporate` AND (representative EQUALS `An officer of the body corporate` OR representative EQUALS `A full-time employee of the party`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (2)(c)
        IF party EQUALS `A partnership` AND (representative EQUALS `A partner of the partnership` OR representative EQUALS `A full-time employee of the party`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (2)(d)
        IF party EQUALS `An unincorporated association` AND (representative EQUALS `A member of the governing body of the unincorporated association` OR representative EQUALS `A full-time employee of the party`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (2)(e) and (3): an individual prescribed by regulations
        IF representative EQUALS `Another individual prescribed by regulations` AND `the regulations prescribe the representative for the party` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations prescribe this individual for this party is not among the sources
        IF representative EQUALS `Another individual prescribed by regulations` AND `the regulations prescribe the representative for the party` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor"
        IF representative EQUALS `An advocate and solicitor` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cannot be represented by an agent, whether paid or otherwise"
        IF representative EQUALS `An agent, whether paid or otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a party to a mediation under this Part (a) must act in person" -- any other representative is outside (2) and (3)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 5(1)(b) and (c) as a regulative rule: a party SHANT be represented by an advocate and solicitor, or by an agent, except as (2) and (3) allow.  The exceptions are the decision function above; this rule is the general prohibition.
-- src:562 | 5.—(1) Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3), a party to a
-- src:563 | mediation under this Part —
-- src:565 | (a) must act in person;
-- src:567 | (b) cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor; and
-- src:569 | (c) cannot be represented by an agent, whether paid or
-- src:570 | otherwise.
@ref s 5(1) (src:562-570)
GIVEN party IS AN `Actor under the Act`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 5(1)(b) the party's prohibition on representation by an advocate and solicitor` MEANS
    PARTY party
    SHANT `be represented by an advocate and solicitor`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "a party to a mediation under Part 2 was represented by an advocate and solicitor"

-- src:562 | 5.—(1) Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3), a party to a
-- src:563 | mediation under this Part —
-- src:565 | (a) must act in person;
-- src:567 | (b) cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor; and
-- src:569 | (c) cannot be represented by an agent, whether paid or
-- src:570 | otherwise.
@ref s 5(1) (src:562-570)
GIVEN party IS AN `Actor under the Act`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 5(1)(c) the party's prohibition on representation by an agent` MEANS
    PARTY party
    SHANT `be represented by an agent`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "a party to a mediation under Part 2 was represented by an agent"

