    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a specified employment dispute listed in a mediation request is unresolved if the dispute — (a) is not settled; and (b) is not withdrawn" (it is settled, or withdrawn)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 6(2): the approved mediator must issue the claimant a claim referral certificate for every unresolved specified employment dispute listed, if (a) the respondent, given reasonable notice, does not attend; (b) no settlement is reached at the end of the mediation; or (c) the mediator is satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement.
