-- src:633 | reasonable prospect of settling through mediation the
-- src:634 | specified employment dispute.
@ref s 6(2) (src:620-634)
GIVEN `section 6 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the dispute is unresolved` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is given reasonable notice of, but does not attend, the mediation for that dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no settlement is reached at the end of the mediation in relation to one or more of the specified employment disputes listed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved mediator is satisfied that there is no reasonable prospect of settling the dispute through mediation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) the approved mediator must issue the claimant a claim referral certificate for the dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" [ruled I(b)] (section 6(1) says section 6 does not apply)
        IF `section 6 applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether section 6 applies was not given
        IF NOT (`section 6 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled I(c)]: the duty is "in respect of every unresolved specified employment dispute"; a dispute that is settled or withdrawn is not spoken to
        IF `the dispute is unresolved` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the dispute is unresolved was not given
        IF NOT (`the dispute is unresolved` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the respondent is given reasonable notice of, but does not attend, the mediation for that dispute` OR `no settlement is reached at the end of the mediation in relation to one or more of the specified employment disputes listed` OR `the approved mediator is satisfied that there is no reasonable prospect of settling the dispute through mediation` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must issue to the claimant a claim referral certificate ... if" (a), (b) or (c); none holds
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

