-- src:727 | resolved by the settlement agreement for mediation
-- src:728 | under this Part (if the settlement agreement arose
-- src:729 | from a mediation under this Part) or for tripartite
-- src:730 | mediation to be conducted by an approved mediator
-- src:731 | (if the settlement agreement arose from a tripartite
-- src:732 | mediation conducted by an approved mediator), with
-- src:733 | or without the consent of the parties to the settlement
-- src:734 | agreement.
@ref s 7(5)(b)(ii) (src:726-734)
GIVEN `a condition in subsection (6) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      origin IS A `Where a settlement agreement arose`
      `the parties to the settlement agreement consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of mediation referred to`
`s 7(5)(b)(ii) the kind of mediation a District Court may refer the dispute to` MEANS
    IF `a condition in subsection (6) is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER origin
         WHEN `From a mediation under Part 2` THEN JUST `Mediation under Part 2`
         WHEN `From a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator` THEN JUST `Tripartite mediation to be conducted by an approved mediator`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [no yes-or-no]: the power is exercised by a District Court that "may, if any condition in subsection (6) is satisfied" do so; none is satisfied, and the function returns a kind of mediation, so there is no JUST FALSE to give
    ELSE NOTHING

