    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a specified employment dispute is unresolved if the dispute is not settled and is not withdrawn by the claimant" (it is settled, or withdrawn)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 7(7)(a): where a District Court sets aside the agreement and refers a dispute for mediation under this Part, the approved mediator must issue the claimant a claim referral certificate for every unresolved dispute so referred, if (i) the respondent, given reasonable notice, does not attend; (ii) no settlement is reached; or (iii) the mediator is satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement.
