      `no settlement is reached at the end of the mediation in relation to one or more of the disputes referred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved mediator is satisfied that there is no reasonable prospect of settling the dispute through mediation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(7)(a) the approved mediator must issue the claimant a claim referral certificate for the dispute referred by the District Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a District Court sets aside ... and refers ... for mediation under this Part, the following apply" [ruled I(b)] (it has not)
        IF (NOT `a District Court sets aside the settlement agreement under subsection (5)(b)(i) and refers the dispute for mediation under this Part under subsection (5)(b)(ii)`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled I(c)]: the duty is "in respect of every unresolved specified employment dispute so referred"; a dispute that is settled or withdrawn is not spoken to
