-- s 7(9): to avoid doubt, where a District Court sets aside the agreement and refers a dispute for tripartite mediation, section 30H(3) to (9) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 applies to it as it applies to a dispute notified under section 30H(2) of that Act.
-- src:794 | (9) To avoid doubt, where a District Court sets aside under
-- src:795 | subsection (5)(b)(i) a settlement agreement, and refers under
-- src:796 | subsection (5)(b)(ii) any specified employment dispute purportedly
-- src:797 | resolved by the settlement agreement for tripartite mediation to be
